WEBVTT

00:00:02.209 --> 00:00:07.110
<v Sarah Okafor>Morning, everyone. Can you hear me? Teams is showing the little spinning thing again.</v>

00:00:09.560 --> 00:00:16.559
<v Grace Liu>Yeah, you're through. Before we start, whose new car is that in the car park? Very shiny for this place.</v>

00:00:17.429 --> 00:00:20.929
<v Jamie Brennan>Not mine. Mine's the one with more dust than paint.</v>

00:00:21.239 --> 00:00:25.089
<v Grace Liu>Someone's parked it miles from everyone else. Give it a week.</v>

00:00:26.230 --> 00:00:31.829
<v Fiona Doyle>Talking of optimism, we've planned a barbecue for the weekend. Weather forecast's changed three times already.</v>

00:00:33.710 --> 00:00:36.509
<v Marcus Hale>So, barbecue under an umbrella. Standard British summer.</v>

00:00:38.659 --> 00:00:40.060
<v Fiona Doyle>Exactly. Sausages in waterproofs.</v>

00:00:42.340 --> 00:00:47.240
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, Wednesday 15 July. Let's get through the actual factory bit before the menu.</v>

00:00:47.840 --> 00:00:53.090
<v Sarah Okafor>First, we finished the repair on the PRV on the boiler last night. That's done.</v>

00:00:54.600 --> 00:00:59.500
<v David Whitfield>Yeah, saw that in the handover. Nice to have that one off the list.</v>

00:00:59.859 --> 00:01:02.659
<v Sarah Okafor>Yep, closed out, not another job for today.</v>

00:01:04.079 --> 00:01:09.680
<v Aisha Begum>And I tested the fire alarm panel yesterday and it's all fine now. That testing's finished.</v>

00:01:10.319 --> 00:01:16.620
<v Grace Liu>I did hear a slight rattle from the fire panel, just so it's mentioned. Nothing to action yet.</v>

00:01:17.310 --> 00:01:21.859
<v Marcus Hale>That's just the noise you're flagging, yeah? Not saying the alarm test failed?</v>

00:01:24.340 --> 00:01:27.489
<v Grace Liu>No, no. Just an observation, not reopening the test.</v>

00:01:29.819 --> 00:01:37.170
<v Grace Liu>Same sort of thing with the GT1 compressor. Noticed it was running a bit warm on nights, but it settled down.</v>

00:01:38.900 --> 00:01:42.750
<v Aisha Begum>Okay, so that settled down, rather than something still climbing now.</v>

00:01:43.170 --> 00:01:46.670
<v Marcus Hale>Yeah. As you say, an observation, not a new call-out.</v>

00:01:48.159 --> 00:01:56.560
<v Aisha Begum>While we're on that equipment, I'll update the risk assessment for work on the GT1 compressor this afternoon. It matters but it's not urgent.</v>

00:01:58.959 --> 00:02:04.560
<v Grace Liu>You mean the work risk assessment, rather than making the warm-running observation into a separate job?</v>

00:02:05.439 --> 00:02:12.090
<v Aisha Begum>Yeah, exactly. I'll update the existing risk assessment for the work. Not raising another job off the temperature comment.</v>

00:02:13.050 --> 00:02:17.250
<v Sarah Okafor>Thanks, Aisha. That's yours this afternoon, then, without treating it as urgent.</v>

00:02:17.580 --> 00:02:23.879
<v David Whitfield>Um, my blocker hasn't moved. The supplier still hasn't confirmed the delivery for the line 1 mould temp.</v>

00:02:25.860 --> 00:02:30.060
<v Jamie Brennan>No confirmed delivery here either. There's nothing definite to put against it.</v>

00:02:32.069 --> 00:02:36.969
<v Fiona Doyle>Right, still blocked. Not putting that down as work we can get through today.</v>

00:02:38.710 --> 00:02:46.409
<v Sarah Okafor>Dave, can you clear the jam and check the sensors on the stretch wrapper by the end of the week? Normal priority.</v>

00:02:48.379 --> 00:02:54.330
<v David Whitfield>Yeah, so both parts of that—clear the jam, then check the sensors, not just get it moving?</v>

00:02:55.129 --> 00:02:58.979
<v Sarah Okafor>Both, please. The sensor check is part of the same job.</v>

00:03:00.449 --> 00:03:08.500
<v David Whitfield>Okay, I'll clear the jam and check the sensors on the stretch wrapper by the end of the week. Normal priority, got it.</v>

00:03:08.900 --> 00:03:12.750
<v Marcus Hale>The old 'it's moving, therefore it's fixed' approach doesn't count, then.</v>

00:03:14.060 --> 00:03:16.860
<v David Whitfield>Sadly not. You've ruined my entire engineering philosophy.</v>

00:03:19.189 --> 00:03:26.889
<v Sarah Okafor>And Dave, can you run a function test on the Compressed Air Dryer on the 3rd? It matters but it's not urgent.</v>

00:03:27.379 --> 00:03:32.280
<v David Whitfield>Sorry, you clipped there. Function test on the Compressed Air Dryer, on the 3rd?</v>

00:03:34.310 --> 00:03:38.509
<v Sarah Okafor>That's right, on the 3rd. Not asking you to bring it forward.</v>

00:03:40.289 --> 00:03:46.939
<v David Whitfield>Yep, accepted. I'll run the function test on the Compressed Air Dryer on the 3rd. Important, but not urgent.</v>

00:03:47.539 --> 00:03:57.340
<v Fiona Doyle>So I've got Dave against the stretch wrapper by the end of the week, normal priority, and the Compressed Air Dryer on the 3rd, matters but isn't urgent.</v>

00:03:59.819 --> 00:04:01.219
<v David Whitfield>That's the pair, yeah.</v>

00:04:02.080 --> 00:04:07.680
<v Sarah Okafor>Next gap: we need someone to book a contractor to look at the GT2 inlet valve.</v>

00:04:08.770 --> 00:04:14.020
<v Fiona Doyle>The booking needs doing on the 3rd. That's the wording I've got, on the 3rd.</v>

00:04:14.789 --> 00:04:19.339
<v Sarah Okafor>Right. Anyone able to take the contractor booking for the GT2 inlet valve?</v>

00:04:21.689 --> 00:04:27.639
<v Jamie Brennan>I can't commit to taking that one. Don't put it against me just because it says contractor.</v>

00:04:29.870 --> 00:04:32.319
<v Marcus Hale>No, I can't take the booking either.</v>

00:04:33.120 --> 00:04:37.670
<v Fiona Doyle>Still unallocated, then. Mentioning the date wasn't me volunteering, just to be clear.</v>

00:04:39.649 --> 00:04:45.949
<v Sarah Okafor>Understood. Contractor booking for the GT2 inlet valve, on the 3rd, still needs doing and has no owner.</v>

00:04:46.600 --> 00:04:52.550
<v Grace Liu>There's another uncovered one: the lock-out tag-out sign-off on the fire panel needs doing at half two.</v>

00:04:53.810 --> 00:05:01.509
<v Aisha Begum>Just—sorry, over you. My fire alarm panel test yesterday isn't that sign-off, and I'm not taking the sign-off by mentioning the test.</v>

00:05:03.819 --> 00:05:08.370
<v Grace Liu>Yeah, separate thing entirely. Yesterday's test is done; this sign-off still needs someone.</v>

00:05:10.029 --> 00:05:14.930
<v Sarah Okafor>Can anyone take the lock-out tag-out sign-off on the fire panel at half two?</v>

00:05:17.009 --> 00:05:18.759
<v David Whitfield>I can't take that one.</v>

00:05:20.399 --> 00:05:25.649
<v Marcus Hale>Nor me. Don't want a nod on a call being read as me accepting it.</v>

00:05:27.449 --> 00:05:34.449
<v Sarah Okafor>Fair enough. No owner for the fire panel sign-off at half two, then. It remains uncovered, not agreed to anybody.</v>

00:05:36.069 --> 00:05:45.170
<v Fiona Doyle>Two unowned items: book the contractor for the GT2 inlet valve on the 3rd, and the lock-out tag-out sign-off on the fire panel at half two.</v>

00:05:47.509 --> 00:05:53.110
<v Grace Liu>And the slight rattle isn't a third item. Still just an observation, nothing to action yet.</v>

00:05:55.430 --> 00:06:02.430
<v Sarah Okafor>Yep. Same for the warm-running comment that settled down. Let's not turn every line in the conversation into another job.</v>

00:06:04.040 --> 00:06:12.439
<v Aisha Begum>My actual commitment is the risk assessment for work on the GT1 compressor. I'll update it this afternoon; it matters but it's not urgent.</v>

00:06:14.839 --> 00:06:24.990
<v David Whitfield>And I've accepted the stretch wrapper jam and sensors by the end of the week, normal priority, plus the Compressed Air Dryer function test on the 3rd, not urgent.</v>

00:06:27.160 --> 00:06:34.509
<v Jamie Brennan>The line 1 mould temp stays in the blocked bit. No delivery confirmation, not a fresh action out of this call.</v>

00:06:35.699 --> 00:06:40.949
<v Fiona Doyle>Yeah, that's clear. Accepted work, unowned gaps, blocked item. Not all one big cheerful list.</v>

00:06:43.360 --> 00:06:49.660
<v Grace Liu>Excellent. Back to the important issue: whoever owns that new car has clearly never met our car park.</v>

00:06:50.709 --> 00:06:54.910
<v Jamie Brennan>Still reckon it's a visitor. Nobody here would risk something that clean.</v>

00:06:56.810 --> 00:07:03.810
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, that'll do. Thanks, everyone. We've got the commitments clear and the two gaps are explicitly unowned. End it there.</v>

00:07:04.970 --> 00:07:06.170
<v Marcus Hale>Cheers, all.</v>
